  "generated_text": "1. **Calculate the modulus of $3-2i$:**\n   The modulus of a complex number $a+bi$ is given by $\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$. For $3-2i$, this is:\n   \\[\n   |3-2i| = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-2)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 4} = \\sqrt{13}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the modulus of $3+2i$:**\n   Similarly, the modulus of $3+2i$ is:\n   \\[\n   |3+2i| = \\sqrt{3^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 4} = \\sqrt{13}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply the moduli:**\n   The product of the moduli is:\n   \\[\n   |3-2i| \\cdot |3+2i| = \\sqrt{13} \\cdot \\sqrt{13} = 13\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   Therefore, the value of $|3-2i|\\cdot |3+2i|$ is $\\boxed{13}$.",
